<newsitem itemid="103781" id="root" date="1996-10-08" xml:lang="en">
<title>UK: Lucas Industries final yr pretax surges.</title>
<headline>Lucas Industries final yr pretax surges.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-10-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year to July 31</p>
<p>			   (million stg unless stated)</p>
<p> Shr (pence, earnings)  12.1		   vs 3.8 loss</p>
<p> Dividend (pence, paid)  7.0		   vs n/a</p>
<p> Pretax before exceps   191.2		  vs 135.8</p>
<p> Pretax after exceps    180.1		  vs 30.4</p>
<p> Turnover		   2,989		  vs 2,796</p>
<p>NOTE - Analysts' had forecast that these, the last 12-month results from Lucas Industries due to its merger to form LucasVarity Plc, would show pretax profits after exceptionals in a range between 175 and 185.4 million stg.  </p>
<p> Operating result	 233		    vs 173</p>
<p> Exceptional charge     11.1		   vs 95 charge</p>
<p> Interest paid	    41.8		   vs 37.2</p>
<p> Tax			  62.9		   vs 53.3</p>
<p> Net taxed		  117.2		  vs 22.9 loss</p>
<p> Attributable	     106.3		  vs 30 loss</p>
<p>NOTE - Lucas paid an second interim dividend earlier this year in advance of these results and, as expected, it declared no further dividend today.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7717</p>
</text>
